  m_text: "TERMS OF SERVICE \nLast Updated: August 9, 2026\n\nWelcome to Marble Blast
    Platinum Unity Port Online (\"Game\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\"). These Terms
    of Service (\"Terms\") govern your use of the Game, including its online services,
    accounts, leaderboards, replay system, and related features.\n\nBy creating an
    account, accessing the online services, or submitting a score to the leaderboards,
    you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree with these Terms, please do not
    use the online services.\n\n1. ELIGIBILITY\n\nYou must be at least 13 years old,
    or the minimum age required to use online services in your country, to create
    an account or use the online leaderboard services.\n\nIf you are under the age
    of majority in your country, you should have permission from your parent or legal
    guardian to use the Game.\n\n2. YOUR ACCOUNT\n\nYou are responsible for maintaining
    the security of your account and for all activity performed through it.\n\nYou
    agree to:\n\n- Provide accurate information when creating an account. - Keep
    your login credentials confidential. - Not share your account with another person.
    - Not use another person's account. - Not create multiple accounts for the purpose
    of gaining an advantage on the leaderboards. - Not sell, trade, transfer, or
    otherwise give your account to another person.\n\nWe may take action against
    accounts that violate these rules.\n\nIf you believe your account has been compromised,
    you should contact us as soon as possible.\n\nUsernames cannot currently be changed
    after registration. Choose your username carefully.\n\n3. LEADERBOARDS\n\nThe
    Game provides online leaderboards that allow players to compare their performance
    with other players.\n\nLeaderboard rankings are intended to represent legitimate
    gameplay.\n\nBy submitting a score, you confirm that the score was achieved in
    accordance with these Terms and the rules of the Game.\n\nWe reserve the right
    to:\n\n- Remove invalid or illegitimate scores. - Remove duplicate or corrupted
    scores. - Correct leaderboard rankings. - Reject scores that cannot be verified.
    - Temporarily hide scores while they are being reviewed. - Suspend or remove
    accounts responsible for fraudulent leaderboard activity.\n\nLeaderboard rankings
    may change as a result of verification, corrections, updates, or other technical
    reasons.\n\n4. CHEATING AND EXPLOITATION\n\nYou may not use any method that gives
    you an unfair advantage over other players.\n\nThis includes, but is not limited
    to:\n\n- Cheats or cheat software. - Bots or automated gameplay. - Macros or
    scripts that automate gameplay. - Memory editing or manipulation. - Modified
    game clients intended to alter gameplay or leaderboard results. - Unauthorized
    third-party programs that modify or interfere with the Game. - Exploiting bugs
    or unintended game mechanics to obtain an illegitimate score. - Manipulating
    network communication or requests to submit fraudulent scores. - Modifying replay
    data to produce a score that was not legitimately achieved. - Any other method
    intended to falsify, manipulate, or circumvent the leaderboard system.\n\nUsing
    an exploit unintentionally does not automatically mean that you have cheated.
    However, knowingly using an unintended mechanic to obtain an unfair leaderboard
    advantage may result in the score being removed.\n\nIf you discover a serious
    exploit affecting the leaderboard, we encourage you to report it rather than
    use it for competitive advantage.\n\n5. REPLAYS\n\nThe Game may record and upload
    gameplay replays associated with leaderboard submissions.\n\nYou understand that:\n\n-
    Replays may be stored on our servers. - Replays may be used to verify leaderboard
    submissions. - Replays may be made available to other players. - We may remove
    replays that are invalid, corrupted, or associated with an illegitimate score.\n\nIf
    a replay cannot be verified or does not accurately represent the submitted score,
    the associated leaderboard entry may be removed.\n\n6. FAIR PLAY\n\nPlayers are
    expected to compete fairly and treat other players with respect.\n\nYou must
    not:\n\n- Harass, threaten, or abuse other players. - Impersonate another player
    or developer. - Attempt to publicly expose another player's private information.
    - Dox or encourage others to dox someone. - Use the leaderboard system to intentionally
    disrupt or target another player. - Submit fraudulent reports against other players.\n\nCompetitive
    disagreement is fine. Personal attacks and harassment are not.\n\n7. USERNAME
    AND USER CONTENT\n\nYou may not use a username, profile information, or other
    user-generated content that:\n\n- Impersonates another person or developer. -
    Contains personal information belonging to another person. - Is intended to harass,
    threaten, or intimidate another person. - Contains illegal or seriously abusive
    material. - Is deliberately designed to circumvent moderation.\n\nWe reserve
    the right to change or remove usernames or other content that violate these Terms.\n\nDespite
    this, usernames cannot currently be changed by the player after registration.\n\n8.
    LEADERBOARD VERIFICATION\n\nSome leaderboard submissions may be automatically
    accepted while others may be subject to additional verification.\n\nWe may use
    information associated with a submission, including gameplay data, replay data,
    account information, and technical information, to determine whether a score
    appears legitimate.\n\nA score being displayed on the leaderboard does not necessarily
    mean that it has been permanently verified.\n\nIf evidence later indicates that
    a score violates these Terms, we may remove or modify it.\n\n9. ACCOUNT AND SCORE
    ENFORCEMENT\n\nDepending on the severity of a violation, we may take one or more
    of the following actions:\n\n1. Remove a specific score. 2. Remove associated
    replay data. 3. Temporarily restrict leaderboard submissions. 4. Temporarily
    suspend an account. 5. Permanently suspend or terminate an account. 6. Remove
    other leaderboard entries associated with the violation.\n\nWe may consider the
    circumstances and severity of each case when determining the appropriate action.\n\n10.
    TECHNICAL ISSUES\n\nWe make reasonable efforts to keep the online services and
    leaderboards available and accurate.\n\nHowever, we do not guarantee that:\n\n-
    The leaderboards will always be available. - Submitted scores will always be
    successfully recorded. - Leaderboard rankings will never contain errors. - Replays
    will always be preserved. - Online services will always be uninterrupted. - Previously
    recorded scores will remain available indefinitely.\n\nTechnical problems, server
    failures, software updates, database errors, or other circumstances may result
    in the loss or alteration of leaderboard data.\n\n11. UPDATES AND CHANGES\n\nWe
    may modify, update, suspend, or discontinue any part of the online services,
    including the leaderboard system, at any time.\n\nWe may also update these Terms
    from time to time.\n\nIf we make significant changes, we may provide notice through
    the Game or another appropriate communication channel.\n\nYour continued use
    of the online services after the updated Terms become effective constitutes acceptance
    of the revised Terms.\n\n12. PRIVACY\n\nYour use of the online services may involve
    the collection and processing of information necessary to provide features such
    as:\n\n- Account authentication. - Leaderboards. - Score submission. - Replay
    storage. - Security and fraud prevention. - Technical support.\n\nFor information
    about how your information is collected, used, and stored, please refer to our
    Privacy Policy.\n\n13. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\n\nThe Game, including its original
    code, artwork, audio, characters, branding, and other original materials, is
    owned by NaCl586 or its respective licensors unless otherwise stated.\n\nYou
    may not copy, redistribute, sell, or commercially exploit our original materials
    without permission, except where expressly permitted by applicable law or a separate
    license.\n\n14. TERMINATION\n\nWe may suspend or terminate your access to online
    services if we reasonably believe that you have violated these Terms or otherwise
    abused the service.\n\nTermination of an account may result in the removal of
    associated leaderboard entries, replays, or other online data.\n\nYou may stop
    using the online services at any time.\n\n15. DISCLAIMER\n\nThe online services
    are provided on an \"as is\" and \"as available\" basis to the extent permitted
    by applicable law.\n\nWe do not guarantee that the services will always be error-free,
    secure, or available.\n\n16. CONTACT\n\nIf you believe a leaderboard score is
    fraudulent, your account has been compromised, or you have another issue regarding
    the online services, please contact us on Discord:\n\nDiscord username: aspergergamer\n\nFor
    leaderboard-related reports, please provide as much relevant information as possible,
    such as:\n\n- Player name - Level - Submitted time - Approximate date of the
    run - Relevant replay or evidence, if available\n\n17. ACCEPTANCE\n\nBy creating
    an account or using the online leaderboard services, you acknowledge that you
    have read, understood, and agreed to these Terms of Service.\n\nHave fun, play
    fair, and keep rolling."
